461 - Be Still, My Soul
 / 
Key: F
Time: 4/4
Tempo: Moderato
Number: 461
Topic: Christian Life - 

Verse 1:
[F/C]Be [C]still, [F/C]my [C7]soul: [F/C]the [C]Lord [F/C]is [Bb]on thy [C]side;
[F/C]Bear [C]patiently [F/C]the [C]cross [F/C]of [Bb]grief or [F/C]pain;
[Am]Leave to thyGod [Dm]to order [C]and provide;
[Gm/D]In every [F/C]change He [Dm]faithful [Gm/D]will remain.
[C]Be [Am]still, mysoul: [Dm]thy best, [C]thy heavenly [Gm/D]friend
[Gm/D]Through [F/C]thornyways leads to [C7/Bb]ajoyful [Dm/A]end.

Verse 2:
[F/C]Be [C]still, [F/C]My [C7]soul: [F/C]thy [C]God [F/C]doth [Bb]undertake
[F/C]To [C]guide [F/C]the [C7]future [C]as [F/C]He [Bb]has the [F/C]past.
[Am]Thy hope, thy [Dm/A]confidence [C]let nothing shake;
[Gm/D]All [F/C]now [Gm/D]mysterious [Dm]shall [Gm/D]be bright at [Gbm/Db]last.
[C]Be [Am]still, my [Dm/A]soul: when waves [C]and winds still [Gm/D]know
[Gm/D]His voice [F/C]who [Gm/D]ruled [F/C]them while [C7/Bb]He dwelth below.

Verse 3:
[F/C]Be [C]still, [F/C]my [C7]soul: [F/C]the [C]hour [F/C]is [Bb]hastening [F]on
[F/C]When [C]we [F/C]shall [C7]be [F/C]forever [Bb]with the [F/C]Lord,
[Am]When disappointment, [Dm]grief, [C]and fear are gone,
[Gm/D]Sorrow [F/C]forgot, love's [Dm]purest [Gm/D]joys restored.
[C]Be [Am]still, my [Dm/A]soul: when change [C]and tears are past,
[Gm/D]All [F/C]safe [Gm/D]and [F/C]blessed we shall [C7/Bb]meet at last.
